WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.969 --> 00:00:20.953
The next day I awoke after sleeping for twelve hours. As usual Conseil came to my room to see if I needed anything.

2
00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:26.103
"Did you sleep well?" he asked as he did every day when we were living on land.

3
00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:29.444
"Quite well," I replied. "Where's Ned?"

4
00:00:29.445 --> 00:00:36.039
"Still sleeping, Master. Ned appears to have plenty of practice at sleeping. He sleeps so soundly that I . . ."

5
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:41.206
Conseil chattered on, but I didn't respond because I was thinking about Captain Nemo.

6
00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:45.864
Why hadn't we seen him last night? I was sure he'd make an appearance today.

7
00:00:45.865 --> 00:00:53.864
As soon as I was dressed, I went into the gallery. It was deserted. I plunged into studying the shells in the glass cases.

8
00:00:53.865 --> 00:00:58.095
I also enjoyed the huge albums filled with rare marine plants.

9
00:00:58.096 --> 00:01:02.762
Even though the plants were dried, they retained their lovely colors.

10
00:01:02.763 --> 00:01:06.595
The whole day passed without Captain Nemo honoring me with a visit.

11
00:01:06.596 --> 00:01:12.920
The panels in the museum room did not open. Perhaps he did not wish us to tire of the beautiful view.

12
00:01:12.921 --> 00:01:19.746
The Nautilus continued on its course, traveling at a depth ranging from 150 to 180 feet.

13
00:01:19.747 --> 00:01:24.817
The next day, November 10, I didn't see a single member of the ship's crew.

14
00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:31.905
Ned and Conseil spent most of the day with me, and they were astonished at the inexplicable absence of the captain.

15
00:01:31.906 --> 00:01:37.984
Was this eccentric man ill? Had he changed his mind about how he was going to treat us?

16
00:01:37.985 --> 00:01:47.135
But as Conseil pointed out, we were still free to roam the submarine and we were always provided with delicious and abundant food.

17
00:01:47.136 --> 00:01:55.294
Our host kept his part of the bargain, and we couldn't complain because this voyage really was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

18
00:01:55.295 --> 00:02:03.127
Early the next morning, November 11, I could smell fresh sea air, so I knew that the Nautilus had risen to the surface.

19
00:02:03.128 --> 00:02:07.723
I went up on the platform, where I fully expected to meet Captain Nemo.

20
00:02:07.724 --> 00:02:13.215
It was six o'clock; the sky was cloudy and the sea was gray but calm.

21
00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:16.778
I saw no one except the pilot in his glass cage.

22
00:02:16.779 --> 00:02:22.857
I inhaled the salt air with delight as the sun's rays gradually burned away the fog.

23
00:02:22.858 --> 00:02:31.111
I was admiring the sunrise when I heard someone climbing up to the platform. I turned, fully expecting to greet Captain Nemo.

24
00:02:31.112 --> 00:02:37.762
But it was only his second-in-command, his lieutenant, the other man that I'd met on our first day onboard the Nautilus.

25
00:02:37.763 --> 00:02:40.945
He climbed onto the platform without seeming to see me.

26
00:02:40.946 --> 00:02:46.008
Putting his telescope to his eye, he scanned the horizon with great attention.

27
00:02:46.009 --> 00:02:53.088
When he'd finished, he went to the hatch and called down, "Nautron respoc lorni virch."

28
00:02:53.089 --> 00:03:01.993
What these words meant I couldn't say, but I have remembered this sentence because he repeated it every day under the exact same conditions.

29
00:03:01.994 --> 00:03:06.493
Having uttered these words, Nemo's lieutenant descended through the hatch.

30
00:03:06.494 --> 00:03:12.246
I thought that the Nautilus was about to resume its underwater voyage, so I went down to my cabin.

31
00:03:12.247 --> 00:03:19.577
Five days passed like this without any change in our situation. Every morning I mounted the platform.

32
00:03:19.578 --> 00:03:26.303
The same man said the same sentence in the same strange language. Captain Nemo did not appear.

33
00:03:26.304 --> 00:03:29.549
I had made up my mind that I would never see him again.

34
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:36.392
But on November 16, I returned to my cabin with Ned and Conseil and found an envelope on my table.

35
00:03:36.393 --> 00:03:42.043
I opened it impatiently and read a note in bold, clear handwriting.

36
00:03:42.044 --> 00:03:44.372
The note was worded as follows:

37
00:03:44.373 --> 00:03:47.622
To Professor Aronnax onboard the Nautilus:

38
00:03:47.623 --> 00:03:56.376
Captain Nemo invites Professor Aronnax to a hunting party that will take place tomorrow morning in his forests on the island of Crespo.

39
00:03:56.377 --> 00:04:00.289
The captain hopes that nothing will prevent the professor from being present.

40
00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:04.110
The professor's companions are also invited to join the hunt.

41
00:04:04.111 --> 00:04:07.361
Captain Nemo, commander of the Nautilus

42
00:04:07.362 --> 00:04:09.844
"A hunt!" exclaimed Ned.

43
00:04:09.845 --> 00:04:14.860
"And in his forests on the island of Crespo!" added Conseil.

44
00:04:14.861 --> 00:04:18.599
"So it sounds like the captain is going ashore," said Ned.

45
00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.931
I read the note again.

46
00:04:20.932 --> 00:04:24.193
"It certainly does seem that way," I said.

47
00:04:24.194 --> 00:04:28.352
"Well, we must definitely accept this invitation," said Ned.

48
00:04:28.353 --> 00:04:32.836
"All this fish is fine, but I wouldn't mind eating some fresh venison."

49
00:04:32.837 --> 00:04:36.431
I was still trying to make sense of Captain Nemo's invitation.

50
00:04:36.432 --> 00:04:41.923
He planned to go hunting in a forest yet had a strong aversion to anything on land.

51
00:04:41.924 --> 00:04:46.836
"I've never heard of this island," I said. "Let's find out where it is."

52
00:04:46.837 --> 00:04:53.487
I consulted the map and showed my companions a tiny island lost in the middle of the northern Pacific.

53
00:04:53.488 --> 00:04:57.820
I also noted that we were about 800 leagues from our starting point.

54
00:04:57.821 --> 00:05:04.320
"If Captain Nemo sometimes does go on dry land," I said, "he certainly chooses remote islands."

55
00:05:04.321 --> 00:05:08.987
The rest of the day passed without another word or visit from the captain.

56
00:05:08.988 --> 00:05:14.384
When I awoke the next morning, I could feel that the Nautilus was perfectly still.

57
00:05:14.385 --> 00:05:19.305
I dressed quickly and entered the gallery, where I found Captain Nemo.

58
00:05:19.306 --> 00:05:27.043
He made no reference to his absence for the past eight days, but simply asked if we would be accompanying him today.

59
00:05:27.044 --> 00:05:37.130
"We will," I replied. "But I'm puzzled by one thing: How can you own forests on Crespo Island if you've cut all ties with land?"

60
00:05:37.131 --> 00:05:46.709
"My forests don't bask in the heat and light of the sun," he replied. "They aren't on land; they're actual underwater forests."

61
00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:52.043
"You're offering to take me to real underwater forests?" I couldn't believe it.

62
00:05:52.044 --> 00:05:57.678
"Yes, Professor, and without getting your feet wet. Now come eat breakfast with me.

63
00:05:57.679 --> 00:06:03.337
There aren't any restaurants on Crespo, and it will be a long time before you have supper."

64
00:06:03.338 --> 00:06:06.941
While we ate, I asked the captain some questions.

65
00:06:06.942 --> 00:06:14.162
"I'm familiar with a diving apparatus that lets a man breathe underwater, but he must stay tethered to a ship," I began.

66
00:06:14.163 --> 00:06:21.288
"Then there's a diving suit that allows a man to leave the ship, but it only contains a limited amount of air in a backpack.

67
00:06:21.289 --> 00:06:23.678
Which one will we be using?"

68
00:06:23.679 --> 00:06:31.662
"A version of the diving suit," said Captain Nemo. "I've improved it so that a man can stay underwater for nine or ten hours."

69
00:06:31.663 --> 00:06:37.987
"But how will we be able to see in the dark waters? And a regular gun won't fire in the water."

70
00:06:37.988 --> 00:06:47.973
The captain smiled. "Don't worry. I've invented both a light and a gun that will work underwater. Are you ready to go hunting?"

71
00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:53.393
We left the dining room and as we passed my companions' cabin, I called for them to join us.

72
00:06:53.394 --> 00:06:58.655
Near the engine room we came to a small room where we found a dozen diving suits.

73
00:06:58.656 --> 00:07:03.631
"Oh no," said Ned. "I'm not getting into one of those."

74
00:07:03.632 --> 00:07:09.528
"But there's no alternative," I said. "The forests of Crespo are underwater."

75
00:07:09.529 --> 00:07:15.456
"Underwater?" Ned seemed to realize that his dream of eating venison was slipping away.

76
00:07:15.457 --> 00:07:21.187
"Unless someone forces me, I won't be going with you," the harpooner replied firmly.

77
00:07:21.188 --> 00:07:25.266
"No one will force you, Mr. Land," said Captain Nemo.

78
00:07:25.267 --> 00:07:28.282
"Are you coming with us?" I asked Conseil.

79
00:07:28.283 --> 00:07:34.532
"I follow my master wherever he goes," replied my loyal servant.
